WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:09.188
Nine walls stand in a row, and you must pick the pair that holds the most water.

00:09.188 --> 00:14.700
Trying every pair means measuring 36 containers.

00:15.000 --> 00:27.572
Instead, start with the widest container: the first and last walls.

00:27.572 --> 00:31.700
Measure what it holds.

00:32.000 --> 00:39.542
The shorter wall is the limit, so move it inward.

00:39.542 --> 00:47.700
Moving the taller wall instead could never hold more.

00:48.000 --> 00:56.979
Each wall moves at most once, so 8 measurements find the best: 49.

00:56.979 --> 00:59.700
That’s two pointers.
